{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304121-how-would-an-owod-mage-see-exalted-reality-ruling-paradigm","id":1304121,"title":"How would an oWoD mage see Exalted Reality/Ruling Paradigm?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-04-11T00:53:37-07:00","id":1304121,"title":"How would an oWoD mage see Exalted Reality/Ruling Paradigm?","content":"This is not vs thread or something I have a legitimate question on how do you think mage would perceive reality within Exalted. I have a short list of a few questions.<br /> <br /> -For one, I think that there is no gauntlet in Exalted so everywhere counts as Shallowing and probably at least a level 1 mystic Node.<br /> -For another, any WoD gains automatic success at any task per spent WP, would it stay same in Exalted where reality is much more pliable? <br /> -Also, fundamental nature of spirits is assumed to be unchangeable in Exalt, while Mage can reshape any spirit with enough successes. Though it would probably be vulgar now. <br /> -The mage would also face less resistance on casting (sphere +2/+3?) and even less paradox due to weaker reality, most probably manifesting as tears into Wyld. <br /> -Do you think immunity to Shaping Attacks would outright block magic or just make it automatically Vulgar? On one hand it is considered fundamentally impossible to overcome, on another mages do exactly that in their home universe with every spell and against much sturdier reality. <br /> -For another, what would Avatar seem closer to for locals? A god? Elemental? Or (as I see) one of the Raksha? <br /> -Do you think exalt Essence is ruled by Spirit, Spirit+Prime or just plain Prime?<br /> -How do you think new rules with mental influence would interact with social charms (+3 diff, high probability of detecting)?<br /> -Do you think Entropy (breaking oaths) and Spirit (namebreaking) would cacel/hijack Oaths and Geasa of Fair Folk and Yozi? How about Unboundable merit? <br /> -Would mortals in Exalted be seen as humans, victors or spirits by WoD mages?<br /> -Is Aggreviated in Exalted and Aggreviated in WoD one and the same thing? <br /> -Would mages that use foci of Celestial Decrees be considered coincidental in Exalted (Wu Lung, Celestial Chorus)? Maybe they would be seen as forgeries?<br /> <br /> *before you mention, I'm also posting this on Mage thread. I'm interested in both points of view.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T01:36:00-07:00","id":1304128,"title":"","content":"Are you asking about MtA characters dropped into Creation, or what kind of Paradigms would mortals in Creation who suddenly Awakened develop?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T02:18:13-07:00","id":1304131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304121-how-would-an-owod-mage-see-exalted-reality-ruling-paradigm?p=1304128#post1304128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you asking about MtA characters dropped into Creation, or what kind of Paradigms would mortals in Creation who suddenly Awakened develop?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> lets say 2 mages from oWoD, each fully educated in mystic and technocratic paradigms correspondingly can experiment in Creation for their hearts content to test out local paradigm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T02:57:23-07:00","id":1304135,"title":"","content":"I think mages would be pretty safe regardless of paradigm. People can do weird shit in Creation. Throw fireballs? Yeah, people do that. Some of them run the place.<br /> <br /> Exalts kind of use a weird combo of Celestial Chorus for the main chunk of their power (except they actually carry a chunk of their gods around with them) with some Akashic Brotherhood stuff slipping in with Martial arts and I suppose Order of Hermes with sorcery? <br /> <br /> And of course mortals with access to sorcery will feel more solidly OOH. Godblooded are kind of CC again, I suppose. <br /> <br /> And of course, Alchies, should they be encountered, are fairly technocratic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T03:10:27-07:00","id":1304136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">double posting.... how do I remove this?</div> </div> </div> </div>I closed the other thread since this one took off. I'd also help with your enquiry but I saw Mage terminology and my eyes glazed over, so I'll leave you in the hands of those better qualified.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T03:31:23-07:00","id":1304138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304121-how-would-an-owod-mage-see-exalted-reality-ruling-paradigm?p=1304135#post1304135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think mages would be pretty safe regardless of paradigm. People can do weird shit in Creation. Throw fireballs? Yeah, people do that. Some of them run the place.<br /> <br /> Exalts kind of use a weird combo of Celestial Chorus for the main chunk of their power (except they actually carry a chunk of their gods around with them) with some Akashic Brotherhood stuff slipping in with Martial arts and I suppose Order of Hermes with sorcery?<br /> <br /> And of course mortals with access to sorcery will feel more solidly OOH. Godblooded are kind of CC again, I suppose.<br /> <br /> And of course, Alchies, should they be encountered, are fairly technocratic.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ah, but there are certain weird things, like spirits/gods having static natures and oaths being inviolate. I think violating those would be vulgar even if not so in WoD itself. For an example, turning fire elemental into wood one is impossible in Exalted as far as I know. Though I agree that Reality in Creation is much weaker, by WoD standards it's more of a Horizon Realm then an universe proper. <br /> <br /> The question I had there, would mage for example be able to learn at least Terrestrial Martial Arts? after all they are common for local supernaturals.<br /> <br /> I don't get what you are saying here.<br /> <br /> Would fit right in for Etherites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","user":"Warpwind","date":". 04-11-2019, 08:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T04:53:19-07:00","id":1304153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304121-how-would-an-owod-mage-see-exalted-reality-ruling-paradigm?p=1304138#post1304138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I don't get what you are saying here.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's possible for non-exalts in creation to learn sorcery. So this wouldn't fit in with the exalt's god-based paradigm, but it matches up with something else they can do. <br /> <br /> Sorry, I'm not hugely familiar with OWoD Mage. Read M20 a couple of times. I'm just trying to map what I can recall onto exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T05:11:58-07:00","id":1304158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304121-how-would-an-owod-mage-see-exalted-reality-ruling-paradigm?p=1304153#post1304153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's possible for non-exalts in creation to learn sorcery. So this wouldn't fit in with the exalt's god-based paradigm, but it matches up with something else they can do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, you mean OoH copying Sorcery? Yeah, emulating it's effects with Spheres would be completely coincidental. However, mages can also learn whatever is considered within current paradigm outright (gen mods, charms, etc.). Furthermore, using local belifes actually provides WoD magics with bonuses. So, if WoD mage used Sorcery appropriate trappings he would receive bonus dice (from medieval mage). <br /> <br /> What I'm more interested though, would they be able to learn Martial Arts? and would successes translate into same effects in different worlds? martial arts carry completely different meaning in WoD and Creation. Or would it function like martial arts foci with bonuses for using local foci. Use M20 rules if you want, np.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T05:34:43-07:00","id":1304161,"title":"","content":"I think, if you were to learn a martial art, you might be able to use spheres to mimic the effects of the charms, or something that could plausibly be a charm, and that would be coincidental.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T05:50:37-07:00","id":1304169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304121-how-would-an-owod-mage-see-exalted-reality-ruling-paradigm?p=1304161#post1304161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think, if you were to learn a martial art, you might be able to use spheres to mimic the effects of the charms, or something that could plausibly be a charm, and that would be coincidental.</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah, that sounds reasonable. I would even add a couple dice for using especially appropriate foci. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T05:53:32-07:00","id":1304170,"title":"","content":"I'm confused at the notion you suggest that spirits are static and unchanging, as Ahlat was once the god of bull walrus mating dances; he certainly didn't look like a Minotaur then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T06:10:26-07:00","id":1304173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304121-how-would-an-owod-mage-see-exalted-reality-ruling-paradigm?p=1304170#post1304170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm confused at the notion you suggest that spirits are static and unchanging, as Ahlat was once the god of bull walrus mating dances; he certainly didn't look like a Minotaur then.</div> </div> </div> </div>Donno. That's what I read in Exalted (can't remember the edition).<br /> For an example, can you take a demon from malfeas and turn it into an elemental with charms? Or for example take a god and merge it with elemental, or make it capable of feeding on blood without falling to underworld?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T06:15:42-07:00","id":1304174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304121-how-would-an-owod-mage-see-exalted-reality-ruling-paradigm?p=1304173#post1304173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Donno. That's what I read in Exalted (can't remember the edition).<br /> For an example, can you take a demon from malfeas and turn it into an elemental with charms? Or for example take a god and merge it with elemental, or make it capable of feeding on blood without falling to underworld?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. <br /> <br /> But it takes effort. Lots of effort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T06:47:30-07:00","id":1304179,"title":"","content":"So thoughts. Now I know Exalted a lot better than I know Mage. But I am at least passingly familiar with Mage.<br /> <br /> First I imagine with high enough Spirit you could at the very least futz about with the Underworld while in Creation and that should probably have some level of Gauntlet unless you are in a Shadowland. But yeah for interacting with Spirits in Creation there would be little if any Gauntlet. I think you could also use Spirit to travel to Yu-Shan or Malfeas without going through traditional means and that would have a Gauntlet rating. There would probably be some incentive (Carrot or Stick) with Malfeas for accepting the five day rule when it comes to travel in or out of the realm.<br /> <br /> Resurrection and Time Travel would both be incredibly vulgar regardless of paradigm.<br /> <br /> I think Charms like Destiny-Manifesting Method would maintain their primacy. So you can do your magic on the Invincible Sword Princess, but even if you turn her into a rock it won't stop her from being the Invincible Sword Princess and that rock could still wreck you. As for the more full stop defenses from previous editon (or Moonsilver tattoos) that I'm less certain of. My gut says they would work against most magic, but that doesn't seem very fun. Of course neither does having no way to defend against the mage. I do however think comparing this to the sturdiness of reality is thinking about it the wrong way. It's not the sturdiness of reality your up against here, it's the spiritual fortitude of the Exalt.<br /> <br /> Random locals would definitely consider the Avatar to be a God. It is THE default assumption when seeing an obviously Supernatural creature that you don't know wha it is. Now when Joe Farmer goes to get an Immaculate Monk or other person who knows what they are talking about it's a different matter. Here I don't feel comfortable giving a definitive answer as my knowledge of Mage avatars is limited. However they do seem more similar to Spirit's of some variety than Fae to me.<br /> <br /> I feel like essence would just be Prime. It feels onehundred percent like something Prime should cover. Now if you are futzing around with another person's Essence that would likely require mixing in Life or Spirit depending on the target.<br /> <br /> Not sure what you mean about Mental Influence.<br /> <br /> Breaking the Yozi Oaths I feel would be incredibly difficult, incredibly Vulgar, require both Spirit and Entropy, and just be an overall bad idea even if you succeeded. As for Fae that seems like it would be a lot easier and maybe not even Vulgar depending on how you do it. But I think it would require some Prime or Life mixed in as well as you are fundamentally changing the nature of a living being (that would not fall under Spirit in my opinion).<br /> <br /> I do not think Mages would see mortals as spirits. The fact that they don't need the Spirit sphere to mess with them would quickly disabuse them of that notion. Beyond that I don't know how Mages would view Exalted's mortals.<br /> <br /> Yeah, Agg is Agg.<br /> <br /> And finally as others have said most traditions would have a very easy time being Coincidental in Creation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304121-how-would-an-owod-mage-see-exalted-reality-ruling-paradigm?p=1304173#post1304173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Donno. That's what I read in Exalted (can't remember the edition).<br /> For an example, can you take a demon from malfeas and turn it into an elemental with charms? Or for example take a god and merge it with elemental, or make it capable of feeding on blood without falling to underworld?</div> </div> </div> </div>With Charms no, not as far as I know. But this is definitely a possibility in Exalted via Sorcerous Workings or other means if incredibly difficult. And Demons of the Second or Third Circles in particular have their own complications, both for Exalted and Mages, as they are in addition to being individuals part of a larger singular entity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/112-sanguine","name":"Sanguine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar112_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T06:49:02-07:00","id":1304180,"title":"","content":"Right, so it would be fairly simple to change one spirit into another spirit of the same type, but a lot harder to change a spirit into a different sort of spirit.<br /> <br /> A god can change, but it's still a god.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T06:51:43-07:00","id":1304181,"title":"","content":"Oh, also given how exalts are a synthesis of mortal and god, They would likely require both life and spirit to affect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T06:57:29-07:00","id":1304183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304121-how-would-an-owod-mage-see-exalted-reality-ruling-paradigm?p=1304180#post1304180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, so it would be fairly simple to change one spirit into another spirit of the same type, but a lot harder to change a spirit into a different sort of spirit.<br /> <br /> A god can change, but it's still a god.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very true. Also this reminded me of something I thought about after posting that comes into this. The additional complication of a God's job. If you change a god in a way that is fundamentally incompatible with their official position within the Celestial Bureaucracy I could see such magic being slowly eroded over time in a similar manner to disbelief. Of course it would have to be a pretty drastic change to be fundamentally incompatible with their position. And it would be open season on the unemployed or forbidden gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/112-sanguine","name":"Sanguine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar112_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T07:48:15-07:00","id":1304188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanguine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304121-how-would-an-owod-mage-see-exalted-reality-ruling-paradigm?p=1304179#post1304179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. First I imagine with high enough Spirit you could at the very least futz about with the Underworld while in Creation and that should probably have some level of Gauntlet unless you are in a Shadowland.</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah, but taking into account underworld shallowings form willy-nilly it would be like what, Gauntlet 3? With spirit 2 you can look across, with spirit 3 reach across. The mages have a couple nasty tricks where they beat up spirits across never actually stepping over. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. But yeah for interacting with Spirits in Creation there would be little if any Gauntlet. I think you could also use Spirit to travel to Yu-Shan or Malfeas without going through traditional means and that would have a Gauntlet rating. There would probably be some incentive (Carrot or Stick) with Malfeas for accepting the five day rule when it comes to travel in or out of the realm. </div> </div> </div>It would probably be Spirit 3 to emulate &quot;Natural&quot; way and Spirit 4+Space 4 to teleport wherever. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. I think Charms like Destiny-Manifesting Method would maintain their primacy. So you can do your magic on the Invincible Sword Princess, but even if you turn her into a rock it won't stop her from being the Invincible Sword Princess and that rock could still wreck you. </div> </div> </div>What is a &quot;Destiny-Manifesting Method&quot;? but besides vampiric lawnchairs had been outlawed by WW anyway. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4. As for the more full stop defenses from previous editon (or Moonsilver tattoos) that I'm less certain of. My gut says they would work against most magic, but that doesn't seem very fun. Of course neither does having no way to defend against the mage.<br /> I do however think comparing this to the sturdiness of reality is thinking about it the wrong way. It's not the sturdiness of reality your up against here, it's the spiritual fortitude of the Exalt. </div> </div> </div>Isn't it the rules of sorcery and reality of essense patterns that dictate such cause and effect? what I really ment was that the shaping immunity/perfect defenses would rather be strong protection that instantly turns any magic affecting it vulgar with witnesses rather then impossible. Because you are doing impossible thing with observer, going against the rules of local reality. So 'perfect' defense would be Exalts spiritual fortitude (essence? willpower?) + charm successes. and of course in WoD in similar situation its mentioned that only supernaturals that actually have similar paradigm can counter mage magic (before M20) like Tremere vs Hermetic or Dreamspeakers vs Werewolves. M20 just makes countermagic flat Wits+Occult for everyone that tries to counter sphere magic. So its debatable what to do here. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 5. However they do seem more similar to Spirit's of some variety than Fae to me. </div> </div> </div>I think it really depends on mage and avatar nature. Having Peter Pen highly Dinamic avatar would be really different then going around with Celestial Dragon pattern avatar. But I was more referring how mystic mages would be quite comfortable at operating in Wyld and that in such places (wyld, undeerworld, malfeas) their avatar becomes overlaid over their physical bodies which would be confusing. Hell with how saturated the Creation is with essence it may manifest all the time.<br /> Also, mage spheres read somewhat similar to Fae shaping effects, mages are just able to affect pretty much anything with it and affect in truth, while fae just do illusions. In return mages are limited by spheres, but not like creation-born would notice THAT difference. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 6. I feel like essence would just be Prime. It feels onehundred percent like something Prime should cover. Now if you are futzing around with another person's Essence that would likely require mixing in Life or Spirit depending on the target. </div> </div> </div>I agree. Interfering with physical bodie's essence is Prime+Life, with spirits it's probably Prime+Spirit for channeling it away or something. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 7. Not sure what you mean about Mental Influence. </div> </div> </div>by M20 supernatural creatures gain WP+3 base difficulty against supernatural compulsion (social charms?), at least 8 with beginner mage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 8. Breaking the Yozi Oaths I feel would be incredibly difficult, incredibly Vulgar, require both Spirit and Entropy, and just be an overall bad idea even if you succeeded. </div> </div> </div>I took idea from medieval infernalists renaming demon lords. and of course is all what you listed, but requires only either Entropy (affect oath itself) or Spirit (rename spirit so the oath doesn't apply to it anymore). Additionally it requires full consent if attempted on powerful spirit and taking into acocunt how resistant Yozi are at changing their fundamental nature - it would be near impossible. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 9. As for Fae that seems like it would be a lot easier and maybe not even Vulgar depending on how you do it. But I think it would require some Prime or Life mixed in as well as you are fundamentally changing the nature of a living being (that would not fall under Spirit in my opinion). </div> </div> </div>In Wyld pretty much everything is coinsidental but what is intrinsic to reality, so oath breaking would still be vulgar and vulgar with witnesses if done within Wyld (manifested by Wyldstorm?). but oaths are a thing in itself, so anything sans' oath-children won't need anyting but Entropy. Raksha aren't really alive anyway, Prime probably would be the sphere used. Or spirit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 10. I do not think Mages would see mortals as spirits. The fact that they don't need the Spirit sphere to mess with them would quickly disabuse them of that notion. Beyond that I don't know how Mages would view Exalted's mortals. </div> </div> </div>The point is that many realms in Umbra are populated by creatures that look perfectly human but are made of ephemera and can never awaken. Really not sure how much mages would consider humans in other universes to actually be 'Human'.<br /> After all, technocracy makes Homo Sapiens in factories (or prints them XD), not to mention all manner of vat-born creatures, near humans and assorted experiments accumulated through ages. So, what is human when you can see souls? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 11. With Charms no, not as far as I know. But this is definitely a possibility in Exalted via Sorcerous Workings or other means if incredibly difficult. And Demons of the Second or Third Circles in particular have their own complications, both for Exalted and Mages, as they are in addition to being individuals part of a larger singular entity. </div> </div> </div>What's a Sorcerous Working? <br /> And that was the other good question. because Mage can erode Sympathies such parts can actually be separated. In Exalted (Return of Scarlet Empress) there is an example of something similar but for DB families. In similar fashion mages can erode (or strengthen) connections between things, voodou doll effect inverted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T08:33:32-07:00","id":1304201,"title":"","content":"Mage would probably ascribe the constellations of Exalted as the Paradigm, since they're a collection of mystic secrets used to cut through or direct the setting. Pattern Spiders would probably be a bigger danger for Namebreakers, though; Sidereals have a professional, working relationship with the spiders, but mages are just unauthorized freeloaders begging to be kicked off or exploded. Willworker beware.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T08:47:12-07:00","id":1304203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304121-how-would-an-owod-mage-see-exalted-reality-ruling-paradigm?p=1304188#post1304188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What's a Sorcerous Working?</div> </div> </div> </div>In third edition, as well as individual spells sorcery also allows you to use a more free-form system to make, well, basically any alteration to reality you can think of, barring certain universal impossibilities.<br /> <br /> The main limitation is that workings take somewhere between a week and several decades, depending on how big the change is and how much sorcery you know. And that bigger effects are more likely to fail.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T08:51:42-07:00","id":1304206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304121-how-would-an-owod-mage-see-exalted-reality-ruling-paradigm?p=1304188#post1304188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> yeah, but taking into account underworld shallowings form willy-nilly it would be like what, Gauntlet 3? With spirit 2 you can look across, with spirit 3 reach across. The mages have a couple nasty tricks where they beat up spirits across never actually stepping over.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It would probably be Spirit 3 to emulate &quot;Natural&quot; way and Spirit 4+Space 4 to teleport wherever.</div> </div> </div> </div>This all sounds legit.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What is a &quot;Destiny-Manifesting Method&quot;? but besides vampiric lawnchairs had been outlawed by WW anyway. </div> </div> </div>Destiny-Manifesting Method is an Integrity Charm in third edition. Basically how it works is when you purchase it you declare what your &quot;destiny&quot; is. Basically the core of your character concept. Things like Ultimate Swordsman or Preeminent Scholar. Then from that point onwards while you can be effected by shaping effects they will never infringe upon your ability to fufill that destiny. A Fae can turn you to stone but if you are the Ultimate Swordsman you will still be able to sword fight even as a statue. It also guarantees there will be someway to undo the effect, even if their otherwise wouldn't be.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Isn't it the rules of sorcery and reality of essense patterns that dictate such cause and effect? </div> </div> </div>Not really. Charms are not really discrete things that exist in setting. They are just a mechanical means of representing the supernatural might of the exalted. An Exalt in setting doesn't have a &quot;Perfect Parry&quot; he's just good enough with a sword to be able to block literally anything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> what I really ment was that the shaping immunity/perfect defenses would rather be strong protection that instantly turns any magic affecting it vulgar with witnesses rather then impossible. Because you are doing impossible thing with observer, going against the rules of local reality. So 'perfect' defense would be Exalts spiritual fortitude (essence? willpower?) + charm successes. and of course in WoD in similar situation its mentioned that only supernaturals that actually have similar paradigm can counter mage magic (before M20) like Tremere vs Hermetic or Dreamspeakers vs Werewolves. M20 just makes countermagic flat Wits+Occult for everyone that tries to counter sphere magic. So its debatable what to do here. </div> </div> </div>Yeah this is a bit of a weird area. So in regards to mystical defenses I would say it would go up against the Exalt's Resolve or Wits+Integrity, possibly with Essence mixed in somehow. It's just more in line with how Exalted operate than going purely off of Essence of Willpower. As for countermagic. Sorcerers should probably be able to do it, if it is restricted.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think it really depends on mage and avatar nature. Having Peter Pen highly Dinamic avatar would be really different then going around with Celestial Dragon pattern avatar. But I was more referring how mystic mages would be quite comfortable at operating in Wyld and that in such places (wyld, undeerworld, malfeas) their avatar becomes overlaid over their physical bodies which would be confusing. Hell with how saturated the Creation is with essence it may manifest all the time.<br /> Also, mage spheres read somewhat similar to Fae shaping effects, mages are just able to affect pretty much anything with it and affect in truth, while fae just do illusions. In return mages are limited by spheres, but not like creation-born would notice THAT difference. </div> </div> </div>Okay I see what your going with here. But a few notes. First the Avatar would probably be immaterial in Creation. Also comfortable in the wyld might be a stretch as they would have to constantly have magic up to protect them from Wyld Mutation. But indeed the deeper you go into the Wyld the easier and less vulgar magic will become.<br /> <br /> Also Fae are not limited to illusions. Especially not in the Wyld.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> by M20 supernatural creatures gain WP+3 base difficulty against supernatural compulsion (social charms?), at least 8 with beginner mage. </div> </div> </div>Ok in that regard I would say only Social Charms with the Psyche keyword (Unnatural Mental Influence in older Editions) would be effected by that, but they definitely would. (Edit: Though how it would be implemented would depend on the base system used. As difficulty means different things in the two systems) Social Charms without the Psyche keyword are not supernatural compulsion though, they are just the Exalt being very persuasive.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Raksha aren't really alive anyway, Prime probably would be the sphere used. Or spirit. </div> </div> </div>I would argue the point about Raksha being alive. But that's neither here nor there. I would accept that life might not be the right sphere for them though. They should not be spirit, it's just not what they are. Prime maybe yeah.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, what is human when you can see souls? </div> </div> </div>You know that will probably actually be really weird for mages what with Exalted Humans having two souls.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What's a Sorcerous Working? </div> </div> </div>Elfive pretty much covered this while I was typing this up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And that was the other good question. because Mage can erode Sympathies such parts can actually be separated. In Exalted (Return of Scarlet Empress) there is an example of something similar but for DB families. In similar fashion mages can erode (or strengthen) connections between things, voodou doll effect inverted. </div> </div> </div>Yeah a Mage can probably do it. It would just be a more involved process than turning a Elemental into a God. It would also almost certainly trigger a chain reaction of unintended consequences in regards to how it changes both the Yozi and the rest of their Soul Hierarchy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":112,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/112-sanguine","user":"Sanguine","date":". 04-11-2019, 11:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/112-sanguine","name":"Sanguine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar112_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T09:08:26-07:00","id":1304212,"title":"","content":"I'd argue that a human in the Exalted setting doesn't quite have two souls, so much as one soul that <i>splits into two</i> after death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T09:09:11-07:00","id":1304213,"title":"","content":"Fair enough","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/112-sanguine","name":"Sanguine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar112_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T10:27:28-07:00","id":1304238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanguine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304121-how-would-an-owod-mage-see-exalted-reality-ruling-paradigm?p=1304206#post1304206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Destiny-Manifesting Method is an Integrity Charm in third edition. Basically how it works is when you purchase it you declare what your &quot;destiny&quot; is. Basically the core of your character concept. Things like Ultimate Swordsman or Preeminent Scholar. Then from that point onwards while you can be effected by shaping effects they will never infringe upon your ability to fufill that destiny. A Fae can turn you to stone but if you are the Ultimate Swordsman you will still be able to sword fight even as a statue. It also guarantees there will be someway to undo the effect, even if their otherwise wouldn't be.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, would an effect that erodes exactly ephemeral concepts like that (e.i. True Faith) work on that? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not really. Charms are not really discrete things that exist in setting. They are just a mechanical means of representing the supernatural might of the exalted. An Exalt in setting doesn't have a &quot;Perfect Parry&quot; he's just good enough with a sword to be able to block literally anything. </div> </div> </div>I admit to not understanding that. because something like &quot;Dat Good&quot; would be covered by Legendary Characteristic+Merit. Charms sound like werewolf gifts to me. An essence matrix fueled by motes, so to day. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah this is a bit of a weird area. So in regards to mystical defenses I would say it would go up against the Exalt's Resolve or Wits+Integrity, possibly with Essence mixed in somehow. It's just more in line with how Exalted operate than going purely off of Essence of Willpower. </div> </div> </div>Sounds reasonable. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for countermagic. Sorcerers should probably be able to do it, if it is restricted. </div> </div> </div>I would agree for High Ritual Magic. but for an example, would it also negate something like plasma-gun shot or cell-hacking app? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Okay I see what your going with here. But a few notes. First the Avatar would probably be immaterial in Creation. Also comfortable in the wyld might be a stretch as they would have to constantly have magic up to protect them from Wyld Mutation. But indeed the deeper you go into the Wyld the easier and less vulgar magic will become. </div> </div> </div>I don't think mages suffer mutations because of their avatar. As I said, in Umbra and other highly spiritually energetic environments (Astral, never-never, soul-society, etc). However, if living too long in such charged place they 'Acclimate' and start having problems with coming back to material reality now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ok in that regard I would say only Social Charms with the Psyche keyword (Unnatural Mental Influence in older Editions) would be effected by that, but they definitely would. (Edit: Though how it would be implemented would depend on the base system used. As difficulty means different things in the two systems) Social Charms without the Psyche keyword are not supernatural compulsion though, they are just the Exalt being very persuasive. </div> </div> </div>sounds good. that would pass under 'subtle influences' in Mage. Though I may have to look into Vamp section, they have a whole discipline for that. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You know that will probably actually be really weird for mages what with Exalted Humans having two souls. </div> </div> </div>Fomori are a thing you know. Although, Exaltation is a soul? Even so, it's not unheard of. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah a Mage can probably do it. It would just be a more involved process than turning a Elemental into a God. It would also almost certainly trigger a chain reaction of unintended consequences in regards to how it changes both the Yozi and the rest of their Soul Hierarchy. </div> </div> </div>Don't Yozi change only if you change their central (Festch?) soul? As far as I remember they regrow 2nd circle souls like people regrow fingernails, no? <br /> I think it would be seen more like robbery from Yozi standpoint. XD <br /> BTW. Inferno is a fascinating place. Am just reading the celestial directions book on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T10:58:01-07:00","id":1304252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304121-how-would-an-owod-mage-see-exalted-reality-ruling-paradigm?p=1304238#post1304238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, would an effect that erodes exactly ephemeral concepts like that (e.i. True Faith) work on that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hard to say. I would say no. Exalted is very clear that defense overrides offense when the two are not compatible. But it's really a measure of which setting conceit you take as preeminent.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I admit to not understanding that. because something like &quot;Dat Good&quot; would be covered by Legendary Characteristic+Merit. Charms sound like werewolf gifts to me. An essence matrix fueled by motes, so to day. </div> </div> </div>They really are not that similar to Werewolf gifts. But I don't know how to really explain them better.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would agree for High Ritual Magic. but for an example, would it also negate something like plasma-gun shot or cell-hacking app? </div> </div> </div>Now someone can correct me if I'm misremembering, I don't have the relevant book on me to check myself. But it is my recollection that in previous editions* Sorcery could be used to counter Alchemical Protocols and vice versa. And well Alchemical Protocols are a very good parallel for your second example. Though I am now imagining the annoyance of a Virtual Adept when they realize electricity isn't readily available in Creation like it is the world of darkness.<br /> <br /> *Protocols have not shown up yet in 3rd Edition so can't say what the rules will be for them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't think mages suffer mutations because of their avatar. As I said, in Umbra and other highly spiritually energetic environments (Astral, never-never, soul-society, etc). However, if living too long in such charged place they 'Acclimate' and start having problems with coming back to material reality now. </div> </div> </div>I will defer to your expertise here. I really don't know enough about how Avatars work to say if they would protect from the Wyld. But the Wyld is very different from the Umbra.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Fomori are a thing you know. Although, Exaltation is a soul? Even so, it's not unheard of. </div> </div> </div>I wasn't referring to the Exalted. I was referring to every single human being in Creation. They have a Hun and a Po. Or an Higher Soul and Lower Soul. If we counted the Exaltation as a Soul it would be 3 for the Exalted. Though as Alucard mentioned you could argue it's one soul that divides on death.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Don't Yozi change only if you change their central (Festch?) soul? As far as I remember they regrow 2nd circle souls like people regrow fingernails, no?<br /> I think it would be seen more like robbery from Yozi standpoint. XD<br /> BTW. Inferno is a fascinating place. Am just reading the celestial directions book on it. </div> </div> </div>Killing their Fetich Soul soul causes them to change into entirely new entities, kind of. But (permanently) killing any Third Circle Soul will cause a Yozi to change in a less dramatic way. Third Circle Demons are literally a fraction of a Yozi's mind. Not a manifestation of it, actually it. Killing them or severing them from a Yozi would by their very nature change that Yozi in some way. They would still be the same entity, Malfeas wouldn't become someone else like Adrian became Adorjan when her Fetich died. But Malfeas would still be changed by the experience. He might lose his love of architecture for instance if you separated/killed that Demon. Second Circle souls have a similar relationship with their progenitor Third Circle. Which would have, a greatly reduced, knock on effect on the Yozi. And yes they will regrow a new Demon, at least with second circles, not as sure with 3rd. But it will be a different person, and thus the composite entity will be at least slightly different.<br /> <br /> Hopefully that was clear. This is a weird and complicated subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/112-sanguine","name":"Sanguine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar112_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T10:58:12-07:00","id":1304253,"title":"","content":"Changing any third circle will alter the yozi. If you kill the fetitch they implode and come back as a totally different being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T11:01:49-07:00","id":1304257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304121-how-would-an-owod-mage-see-exalted-reality-ruling-paradigm?p=1304201#post1304201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage would probably ascribe the constellations of Exalted as the Paradigm, since they're a collection of mystic secrets used to cut through or direct the setting. Pattern Spiders would probably be a bigger danger for Namebreakers, though; Sidereals have a professional, working relationship with the spiders, but mages are just unauthorized freeloaders begging to be kicked off or exploded. Willworker beware.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, mages that awakened within Creation would of course use local paradigm. Pattern Spiders exist in WoD, and in much greater numbers, and are a standard force of Paradox.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304121-how-would-an-owod-mage-see-exalted-reality-ruling-paradigm?p=1304253#post1304253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changing any third circle will alter the yozi. If you kill the fetitch they implode and come back as a totally different being.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, missed that I guess. So I guess the sympathy between 3rd circle and Yozi is like with body part and with 2nd circle like with a child?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","user":"Warpwind","date":". 04-11-2019, 02:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T11:22:03-07:00","id":1304266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304121-how-would-an-owod-mage-see-exalted-reality-ruling-paradigm?p=1304257#post1304257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, mages that awakened within Creation would of course use local paradigm. Pattern Spiders exist in WoD, and in much greater numbers, and are a standard force of Paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I mean that the Loom of Fate would punish anyone who used Special K to deviate from it, and doing anything coincidental is going to require both knowledge of the system and a rather large amount of paperwork. Also, Pattern Spiders from the WoD were not even remotely the same thing as what Pattern Spiders in Exalted became.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T11:26:13-07:00","id":1304269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanguine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304121-how-would-an-owod-mage-see-exalted-reality-ruling-paradigm?p=1304252#post1304252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hard to say. I would say no. Exalted is very clear that defense overrides offense when the two are not compatible. But it's really a measure of which setting conceit you take as preeminent.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, how do they deal with that In Setting? I mean if everyone was invunerable/immortal how do exalted get killed in game? or during first age?<br /> Furthermore, is that an AOE effect? as in, does it cancel effect aimed at space around Exalted, instead of Exalted itself? <br /> Also, is that from 3rd edition?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They really are not that similar to Werewolf gifts. But I don't know how to really explain them better. </div> </div> </div>That's ok, I'll look in mechanics if nobody pops-up. <br /> <br /> [QUOTE] Now someone can correct me if I'm misremembering, I don't have the relevant book on me to check myself. But it is my recollection that in previous editions* Sorcery could be used to counter Alchemical Protocols and vice versa. And well Alchemical Protocols are a very good parallel for your second example. Though I am now imagining the annoyance of a Virtual Adept when they realize electricity isn't readily available in Creation like it is the world of darkness.[QUOTE]<br /> But wouldn't in the same way as Electricity=/=Elemental Lightning the Alchemical Protocols =/= Chemistry or physics? Also, VA have quite am experiense working with awakened computers (their small god is awake) or with ones boosted by spells. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I will defer to your expertise here. I really don't know enough about how Avatars work to say if they would protect from the Wyld. But the Wyld is very different from the Umbra. </div> </div> </div>Umbra is a catch-all term. For example - Low Umbra=Underworld, High Umbra=Heaven, Middle Umbra is overlaid with Creation (elementals, terrestrial gods).<br /> Wyld would be analogous to Dreaming I think. <br /> Though you could, if you want to, treat it like Awakening treats Amnionic winds (if I remember term correctly) and have player roll Arete+Avatar reflexively after some intervals. Otherwise it's after around 3 months of un-shielded exposure (if I remember correctly) that they are in trouble. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I wasn't referring to the Exalted. I was referring to every single human being in Creation. They have a Hun and a Po. Or an Higher Soul and Lower Soul. If we counted the Exaltation as a Soul it would be 3 for the Exalted. Though as Alucard mentioned you could argue it's one soul that divides on death. </div> </div> </div>Hun and Po are also present in WoD. Westerners know them under Shadow and Daimon. I mean, even IRL some psychologists and phylosophers are heavy on that, like Jung with with his exploration of Shadow/Po and Socrates with his communions with Daimon/Hun. Not to mention, Avatars can aso have another one attached to it. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Killing their Fetich Soul soul causes them to change into entirely new entities, kind of. But (permanently) killing any Third Circle Soul will cause a Yozi to change in a less dramatic way. Third Circle Demons are literally a fraction of a Yozi's mind. Not a manifestation of it, actually it. </div> </div> </div>I agree about that. No wonder they are so damaged. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Second Circle souls have a similar relationship with their progenitor Third Circle. Which would have, a greatly reduced, knock on effect on the Yozi. And yes they will regrow a new Demon, at least with second circles, not as sure with 3rd. But it will be a different person, and thus the composite entity will be at least slightly different. </div> </div> </div>thanks for explanation!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T11:29:08-07:00","id":1304270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304121-how-would-an-owod-mage-see-exalted-reality-ruling-paradigm?p=1304266#post1304266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, I mean that the Loom of Fate would punish anyone who used Special K to deviate from it, and doing anything coincidental is going to require both knowledge of the system and a rather large amount of paperwork. Also, Pattern Spiders from the WoD were not even remotely the same thing as what Pattern Spiders in Exalted became.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am reading it and Loom of Fate isn't punishing anyone. it's a monitoring system as far as I can see. It's sidereals and patterns spiders that do the action. <br /> So how do the Pattern Spiders in two universes differentiate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T12:04:31-07:00","id":1304281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304121-how-would-an-owod-mage-see-exalted-reality-ruling-paradigm?p=1304269#post1304269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, how do they deal with that In Setting? I mean if everyone was invunerable/immortal how do exalted get killed in game? or during first age?<br /> Furthermore, is that an AOE effect? as in, does it cancel effect aimed at space around Exalted, instead of Exalted itself?<br /> Also, is that from 3rd edition?</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally there are limitations on the defenses. If my attack that always hits goes up against your defense that always protects than you win that clash of unstoppable vs immovable. But neither of us can do this forever. In practice you can't perfect defend against every attack. At least with traditional attacks. Now with Shaping it's a bit easier, Destiny-Manifesting Method is permanent after all. But even there there is the idea that if you go long enough without using your guaranteed means of ending the effect, which is not guaranteed to be easy, you will eventually die from lethal things like being turned to stone.<br /> <br /> So to answer your question. They're not actually invulnerable. They are just capable of parrying a mountain that is thrown at them if they exert themselves. Or similarly impressive feats of defense.<br /> <br /> And no generally these are not area of effect. And with shaping defenses in particular they have frequently been explicitly stated to not prevent environmental changes that put you at risk. Only direct changes to your person.<br /> <br /> And the primacy of defense over offense is explicit in second edition. I can't find it explicitly mentioned in third edition. Though many defenses in 3rd edition do say thye defend against the indefensible in various ways. (Eg Block the Unblockable, Dodge the Undodgeable, etc.)<br /> <br /> It's also worth noting here that the phrase &quot;perfect defense&quot; is not used in third edition and there closest equivalents are a lot less perfect than in previous editions. Though they are still exceptionally good against &quot;uncountable damage&quot; and &quot;shaping effects.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But wouldn't in the same way as Electricity=/=Elemental Lightning the Alchemical Protocols =/= Chemistry or physics? Also, VA have quite am experiense working with awakened computers (their small god is awake) or with ones boosted by spells. </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah Electricity is still around. I was just commenting that the lack of existing infrastructure to harness it would be an annoyance to a Virtual Adept that wasn't expecting it. But nothing more than an annoyance. As for Alchemical Protocols being physics. Only in the way that Technocracy magic is physics, heck arguably less than that. It is very much a supernatural rewriting of reality.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Umbra is a catch-all term. For example - Low Umbra=Underworld, High Umbra=Heaven, Middle Umbra is overlaid with Creation (elementals, terrestrial gods).<br /> Wyld would be analogous to Dreaming I think.<br /> Though you could, if you want to, treat it like Awakening treats Amnionic winds (if I remember term correctly) and have player roll Arete+Avatar reflexively after some intervals. Otherwise it's after around 3 months of un-shielded exposure (if I remember correctly) that they are in trouble. </div> </div> </div>The Dreaming is indeed the best analogue in WoD to the Wyld but even then it's not a perfect one. For a lot of reasons. Both in terms of how it operates and just in general what it is. The Wyld is not a different realm of Existence like Heaven, Hell, or the Underworld. You can just walk there with no magic involved. But moving away from metaphysics, the Amnionic Winds thing seems like a good way of dealing with it's mutagenic properties.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> thanks for explanation! </div> </div> </div>You're welcome.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/112-sanguine","name":"Sanguine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar112_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T12:52:01-07:00","id":1304294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanguine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304121-how-would-an-owod-mage-see-exalted-reality-ruling-paradigm?p=1304281#post1304281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> snip<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>thanks for clearing that up! really helped!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T13:23:42-07:00","id":1304305,"title":"","content":"The Dreaming is only part of the inspirational material that went into Exalted's Wyld; Werewolf's Wyld is also part of it, and the mutagenic effects are akin to becoming like one of the gorgons from Werewolf, only without separate spirits of the Wyld to make it happen (and they would reject humans anyway in W:tA).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304121-how-would-an-owod-mage-see-exalted-reality-ruling-paradigm?p=1304270#post1304270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am reading it and Loom of Fate isn't punishing anyone. it's a monitoring system as far as I can see.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even Sidereals, who are authorized to make alterations to the Loom within the boundaries of Astrology, can easily get clapback and resistance from the Pattern Spiders that maintain it. Someone who lacks these credentials is probably going to end up in more trouble than just an occasional Pattern Bite.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's sidereals and patterns spiders that do the action.<br /> So how do the Pattern Spiders in two universes differentiate? </div> </div> </div>Exalted Pattern Spiders are automaton-gods that cover the passage of destiny.<br /> <br /> W:tA Pattern Spiders were Weaver-spirits that spun the Gauntlet up and kept matter apart from spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T13:42:51-07:00","id":1304312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304121-how-would-an-owod-mage-see-exalted-reality-ruling-paradigm?p=1304305#post1304305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Even Sidereals, who are authorized to make alterations to the Loom within the boundaries of Astrology, can easily get clapback and resistance from the Pattern Spiders that maintain it. Someone who lacks these credentials is probably going to end up in more trouble than just an occasional Pattern Bite.</div> </div> </div> </div>that is still pattern spiders attacking, not the Loom itself. also, paradox level varies from 'occasional pattern bite' to 'frozen forever in stasis' to 'exploded violently' to 'abducted for torture'. The difference I can see is these spiders would respond to Entropy or Time paradox rather then Spirit. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Exalted Pattern Spiders are automaton-gods that cover the passage of destiny. </div> </div> </div>As I can see Destiny in Exalted covers cause-and-effect as well as passage of time and proper interaction. In other words - order. So both are pattern alligned spider spirits creating and protecting order. If there is some other functional difference I would be glad to hear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T16:20:57-07:00","id":1304335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304121-how-would-an-owod-mage-see-exalted-reality-ruling-paradigm?p=1304312#post1304312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">that is still pattern spiders attacking, not the Loom itself. also, paradox level varies from 'occasional pattern bite' to 'frozen forever in stasis' to 'exploded violently' to 'abducted for torture'. The difference I can see is these spiders would respond to Entropy or Time paradox rather then Spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's just the thing - they don't parse the world in Spheres, but into Colleges, and to them, Paradox is Paradox.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As I can see Destiny in Exalted covers cause-and-effect as well as passage of time and proper interaction. In other words - order. So both are pattern alligned spider spirits creating and protecting order. If there is some other functional difference I would be glad to hear. </div> </div> </div>Exalted Pattern Spiders are: Born of a designed god, keep a flexible system functioning when the Maidens don't want to make it work, don't like to work more than they have to, and have a single, definite progenitor, which was built by Autochthon.<br /> <br /> Werewolf Pattern-spiders are: Born of a fractured desire for absolute understanding held by the Weaver, totally dedicated to freezing everything forever to make this a reality, and far greater in number because they, like banes, are born of a pathological desire harbored by a Triatic spirit. Also, not mechanical or automatons, just spirits; machine-spiders are a different kind of Weaver-spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T19:04:58-07:00","id":1304373,"title":"","content":"A few points that seem to be missed about the Exalted setting:<br /> <br /> <br /> In Exalted, there is no Gauntlet, and no spirit world/umbra at all. Spirits exist fully in whatever location they are at. In creation, the spirit may be dematerialized, but it is still physically present within creation. The Underworld, Autothonia, Malfeas, and Yu-Shan are completely different planes of existence that have gateways between them and Creation. Same with spirit sanctums. Don't even get me started on Elsewhere! The Wyld is a physical location. There is no outer space, and the sun and moon are physical objects that actually fly between the surface of creation and the adamantine dome upon which the stars are mounted. So MtA mechanics concerning the Gauntlet and Umbra simply don't apply in Exalted as written. There's nothing wrong with homebrewing rules to use a similar system. But the difficulty to travel between planes of existence should be pretty darned high in most places. Correspondence and Spirit should both be required for most travel of this kind.<br /> <br /> (The following is based on Ex2 material, all my be changed in Ex3.) In Exalted, the rules of reality are defined by the Loom of Fate. While there are MANY uses for the Loom, it was created to define the rules of creation. Because of the Loom, gravity works, fire is hot, etc. The only way to bend or break the rules of reality is using essence or disrupting it with the Wyld. In the time of Exalted, the Loom is MUCH stronger than in the OWoD, the Incarnae that created it (the Maidens) still take a hand in maintaining it, and there are exponentially more pattern spiders running around keeping all those f^&amp;%ing essence wielders from ruining the Loom. The reason that the world of Exalted appears to be less stable is because of all the essence being used everywhere. Spirits use essence. Exalted use essence. Mortal sorcerers and martial artists use essence. Manses use essence. Shadowlands leak underworld essence. So the Loom is under constant stress and the greater number of pattern spiders are still stressed out keeping things together.<br /> <br /> (Based on Ex1, where Creation was an ancient precursor to the OWoD) In the OWoD, the spirits have been mostly locked away in the spirit world, and there are no other forms of essence wielder to mess with the Loom. The Wyld is sealed away from creation by the Gauntlet and the Horizon. Malfeas and the Underworld are also sealed away. Gods no longer interfere in the daily operation of creation. So the greatly diminished Pattern Spiders can manage to keep the Loom from failing. The Mages of the OWoD are really the last big annoyance to the Pattern Spiders, and their are enough Spiders around to respond when they catch Mages tampering with the Loom. .)<br /> <br /> So the real question is &quot;How does MtA magic work in terms of Exalted?&quot; Is it all shaping? Is it a form of essence manipulation? Does the Mage have a bit of raw Wyld in his soul, allowing him to manipulate reality? Are Mages within Fate or outside of Fate? Obviously there is no cannon answer, but you need to decide the answer for your story. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/472-keldorn2198","name":"Keldorn2198","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-12T07:21:43-07:00","id":1304439,"title":"","content":"The last post kind of gets into a fundamental thing to remember with anything crossover-related. That being you have to kind of establish what your goals are (like, what do you wnat Mages to be, how much do you think they <i>should</i> warp the setting), and then you have to no matter what comrpomise or change one or both settings involved in order for the crossover to function.<br /> <br /> In the case of a Mage and Exalted, there's a big range between them being able to manipulate the world, even setting-rules-brekaingly, on one end. And on another, it could be argued that the nature of reality in Creation is just not compatable with the WIllworking of a mage, and that their insights on the Spheres doesn't actually matter as they're in effect applying the wrong programming language to the wrong system, to use the metaphor. There's a lot inbetween, but I think regardless something often gets compromised in crossovers, especially when they ahve pretty deep setting mechancis that fundementally don't just take things differently, but in contradicotry ways.<br /> <br /> I think that this is a bit that the OP kind of missed. It just kind fo starts dropping Mages in and making changes. So far, most seem to be towards the Mage side, so I'm guessing Mage is the &quot;right&quot; one when possible, yes? Is the plan to recast Creation in a Mage-compatable light, or is it to make a new setting where Mages can operate in Creation? Those are going to be different results and I think probably needs to be pointed out to help on this stuff, since I see a lot of trying to explain Creation in light of assumptions that shared terms mean th same thing accross settings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-12T08:16:04-07:00","id":1304441,"title":"","content":"Well, the OP asked for Creation as viewed as a mage paradigm. <br /> <br /> &quot;How would you construct OWoD mages using exalted rules?&quot; is a fundamentally different question. And one I'd have much more trouble answering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-12T13:19:16-07:00","id":1304491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And on another, it could be argued that the nature of reality in Creation is just not compatable with the WIllworking of a mage, and that their insights on the Spheres doesn't actually matter as they're in effect applying the wrong programming language to the wrong system. </div> </div> </div>Let's say we have a different understanding how Mage works and leave it at that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think that this is a bit that the OP kind of missed. It just kind fo starts dropping Mages in and making changes. So far, most seem to be towards the Mage side, so I'm guessing Mage is the &quot;right&quot; one when possible, yes? </div> </div> </div>there is a whole fan-made supplement for Exalts in WoD so I didn't see any point in investigating that alley. I am also way more familiar with Mage then Exalt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-12T13:41:46-07:00","id":1304498,"title":"","content":"Yeah, &quot;magic as reality programming&quot; is more an awakening thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T01:20:03-07:00","id":1305419,"title":"","content":"for those that are interested, I came about this interesting discussion that starts with D&amp;D vs Exalted and quickly dips into basically Vulgar vs Coincidental for shaping effects argument.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forums.spacebattles.com/threads/an-e3-solar-circle-exalted-vs-a-level-12-15-adventuring-party-d-d.268966/page-2\" target=\"_blank\">https://forums.spacebattles.com/thre....268966/page-2</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T08:53:55-07:00","id":1305489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanguine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304121-how-would-an-owod-mage-see-exalted-reality-ruling-paradigm?p=1304206#post1304206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You know that will probably actually be really weird for mages what with Exalted Humans having two souls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly. The higher x lower soul dichotomy of Creation maps quite cleanly into the Hun x Po' / &quot;Self&quot; x Shadow arrangement from oWoD.<br /> <br /> Ah, already adresssed in far greater detail than i could muster. That's what i get for commenting before reading all the thread, my bad.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304121-how-would-an-owod-mage-see-exalted-reality-ruling-paradigm?p=1304441#post1304441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the OP asked for Creation as viewed as a mage paradigm.<br /> <br /> &quot;How would you construct OWoD mages using exalted rules?&quot; is a fundamentally different question. And one I'd have much more trouble answering.</div> </div> </div> </div>As either an sketchy first draft or brokenly cobbled together hodge-podge of sidereal Fate-Weaving and Alchemical Protocols.<br /> Its arrangement and the whole subject of Paradox in oWoD scream of a terribly buggy system shaping the underpinings of reality.<br /> <br /> What makes some sort of crossover sense i guess, as Awakened magic is based on the idea of the avatar as broken fragment of whatever the Pure Ones were...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 04-17-2019, 12:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T13:58:39-07:00","id":1305550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304121-how-would-an-owod-mage-see-exalted-reality-ruling-paradigm?p=1305489#post1305489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not exactly. The higher x lower soul dichotomy of Creation maps quite cleanly into the Hun x Po' / &quot;Self&quot; x Shadow arrangement from oWoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>It maps less cleanly onto it than you might think, as ghosts in the WoD don't actually divide into two on death. Only Hungry Dead really split apart that way. Also, the Five Phases are slightly off for the setup in Creation, since Air is only kind of like Metal (associated with the po) in some respects, but Air has associations with lightning instead of Wood (associated with the hun in the Wu Xing's setup) and cold instead of Water and so now everything is crazy without principles of Yin and Yang.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T06:14:22-07:00","id":1305713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304121-how-would-an-owod-mage-see-exalted-reality-ruling-paradigm?p=1305550#post1305550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It maps less cleanly onto it than you might think, as ghosts in the WoD don't actually divide into two on death. Only Hungry Dead really split apart that way. Also, the Five Phases are slightly off for the setup in Creation, since Air is only kind of like Metal (associated with the po) in some respects, but Air has associations with lightning instead of Wood (associated with the hun in the Wu Xing's setup) and cold instead of Water and so now everything is crazy without principles of Yin and Yang.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The concept is very much there thought the &quot;physical&quot; split in two separate beings itself does not occur. Also, the elemental associations model for oWoD are secondary at best, as even in it they are not universally accounted for or considered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T07:44:36-07:00","id":1305724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304121-how-would-an-owod-mage-see-exalted-reality-ruling-paradigm?p=1305713#post1305713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The concept is very much there thought the &quot;physical&quot; split in two separate beings itself does not occur.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that it's not quite the same when that full split doesn't occur.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, the elemental associations model for oWoD are secondary at best, as even in it they are not universally accounted for or considered. </div> </div> </div>It gets slightly more important in EX3, since there was an attempt made to produce a sorcerous initiation that used some elements of traditional Chinese medicine, namely the organ system correspondences, and the lungs, normally associated with Metal, are in Exalted, associated with Air.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T10:01:55-07:00","id":1305746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304121-how-would-an-owod-mage-see-exalted-reality-ruling-paradigm?p=1305724#post1305724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except that it's not quite the same when that full split doesn't occur.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It gets slightly more important in EX3, since there was an attempt made to produce a sorcerous initiation that used some elements of traditional Chinese medicine, namely the organ system correspondences, and the lungs, normally associated with Metal, are in Exalted, associated with Air.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The matter of elemental correspondences could change between regions from southeast asia, so the differences might matter far less than you guess. <br /> \u200b<br /> And again, this is a matter of chinese medicine correspondence with Creation than oWoD x Creation, as the role of the elemental correspondences would be of questionanle relevance depending from what side of the oWoD are you checking. Broken bases or model conflicts all the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-28T11:02:39-07:00","id":1308488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304121-how-would-an-owod-mage-see-exalted-reality-ruling-paradigm?p=1305713#post1305713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The concept is very much there thought the &quot;physical&quot; split in two separate beings itself does not occur. Also, the elemental associations model for oWoD are secondary at best, as even in it they are not universally accounted for or considered.</div> </div> </div> </div>separation occurs only in the souls broken in hell [e.i hungry ghosts], removing it artficicially would make someone a complete pushover pacifist, a bad idea in WoD. Also, some splats like Kuei-jin use Po for cetrain disciplines like demon shintai.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-28T11:09:07-07:00","id":1308490,"title":"","content":"They also might see the populous as all having a version of the Nephalim Merit, since it is clear that the mortals are far closer to their spiritual side in Creation than those in the WoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T05:53:47-07:00","id":1308656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304121-how-would-an-owod-mage-see-exalted-reality-ruling-paradigm?p=1308490#post1308490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They also might see the populous as all having a version of the Nephalim Merit, since it is clear that the mortals are far closer to their spiritual side in Creation than those in the WoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>nope. that would be God-Blooded merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}